Z||000026||JBGehling||05-16-2001||08:27 AM||||One really funny rumor I've heard at school is the reason I have three fieros is because they get so hot I can't drive a single one for too long  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. lol. <BR>Another one is that the fiero has no cooling system. sigh. Finally, some people tell me the reason they catch on fire is because there are no hood vents on the car!<P>Oh well... at least most people think it's a really beautiful car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!<P>Josh||||reg||1
Z||000027||Hartz||05-16-2001||10:47 AM||||On the topic of people not recognizing/believing Fieros are Pontiacs - I had a near "incident" in the parking lot of a GM assembly plant one morning when I parked my '85 SE.  This was back in the 80's when the "Buy American" thing was quite strong, and there were lots of signs up reminding people that parking in the lot was for "American Cars Only."  Three rather burly looking gentlemen came over to remind me of this fact.  I had to walk them around to the rear of the car where PONTIAC was stamped into the back bumper before they'd believe me.  <P>Amazing...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I'll give them the benefit of the doubt and say that the air dam and spoilers threw them off, but still...<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||7
